Autofocus, manual exposure and state-keeping patches for libcamera 0.7.2's
software ISP (simple pipeline), applied by libcamera-pro1x after the two
sensor patches in ../.

Origin: moWerk's SailfishOS mainline port of the Pro¹x,
github.com/moWerk/sailfishos-pro1x-mainline, patches/libcamera/, commit
67ee012 (2026-10-30), copied unchanged.
- 0004-0009: Milan Zamazal's softisp autofocus series, posted to the
  libcamera list (Signed-off-by in each patch); 0009 is moWerk's backport
  to 0.7.2.
- 0010-0017: moWerk's (sharpness value, configurable scan, manual AGC,
  AfWindows, gstreamer AfState, refocus rule, crop centring, keeping
  exposure/colour/focus over a camera restart).
- 0018 (ours): longer exposures, the vertical blanking raised.  Our 0019
  (faster auto exposure) was dropped: with it, tap to focus at 50 cm
  never focused (moWerk, 2026-11-08).
- 0020, 0021 (ours, 2026-11-16): manual lens position (AfModeManual and
  LensPosition, for a focus slider) and spot metering on the autofocus
  area (AeMeteringMode spot, for exposure at a tap).
- 0022 (ours, 2026-11-16): AwbEnable false keeps the white balance gains (a
  lock), also over a camera restart for a photo.
- 0023 (ours, 2026-11-16): above 2% of samples coming out white the
  exposure aims lower, by at most two stops (a lamp in a dim room was left
  white).  White counts from the raw level that clips after the white
  balance gains (2026-11-17; the top bin alone missed it under a lamp).
- 0024 (ours, 2026-11-17): libcamerasrc names the 10-bit CSI-2 packed Bayer
  formats (rggb10p ...), so the simple pipeline's raw stream can be a pad:
  the camera app's photos come from it.
- 0025 (ours, 2026-11-17): frames over 24 MP get two buffers instead of
  four (48 MP: 0.73 GB in use instead of 1.85, with the camera app's 7936
  width that libcamerasrc need not copy).  The count follows the mode
  when validated again: libcamerasrc validates the 48 MP default first,
  and two buffers for the 12 MP viewfinder plus raw stream stalled both
  after one frame (fixed the same day; both cameras then 15-17 fps).
Their 0001 (old kernel headers) and 0002/0003 (sensor helpers, ours are
../s5k4h7-sensor.patch and ../imx582-sensor.patch) are not used.
Licence: libcamera is LGPL-2.1-or-later; these patches modify it.  The
source repository states no licence of its own.

The Af block in ../imx582.yaml is moWerk's, measured on their unit.

State: applies cleanly on Guix's libcamera 0.7.2 with our sensor patches
(2026-10-30).  On the phone (deploy, 2026-10-30): cam lists both cameras,
captures 20 rear frames without error, and the rear camera exposes AfMode
(continuous by default), AfWindows, AfMetering, ExposureTime(Mode),
AnalogueGain(Mode) and ExposureValue.  Focus quality in Snapshot: untested.
